module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.WordTraps

/-!
# Traps for 232 blocks of period 14, from the locked windows of 16 cells carried leftward

The census of locked windows of 16 cells at periods 10 to 15 finds, for every block, the bottom components of its
locked windows, closed sets of windows on which column 1 is fixed at the white phases, and the chain of columns that
each fixes to its left. At period 14 those chains hold 232 blocks that no other trap module has, that nothing
excludes, and that a component of at most 3,000 states reaches. Here each is the component of least cost carried to
the block, a trap of 126 to 174 states and 17 to 104 cells, which the kernel checks one
declaration each.

* `cen<block>`, `cen<block>_check`: the traps, each passing the check of [WordTraps](WordTraps.md).
* `censusTraps14`, `censusTraps14_check`, `censusTraps14_blocks`: the list, its check and its blocks.
* `census14_absorption_excludes`: for each of them, if every finitely supported right half driven by the block
  enters its trap, the center column does not eventually repeat the block.

The tables come from `python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-census 14`. The natural-language argument is
`CensusTraps14.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata

